From 14845fed5ae7bf7abefdaa33e12981de3188c6c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:35:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/29] macOS: choose the Mac builds; run them on a Mac of your
 own

A Mac build ran two GitHub Mac machines (Intel and Apple Silicon) at
about ten times the Linux rate, roughly 600-700 of the Free plan's
2,000 minutes, even for a user whose Macs are all Intel.

- The form has "Mac builds" for macOS: Intel and Apple Silicon (the
  default), Intel only, or Apple Silicon only. It goes to the workflow
  as the optional input mac_arch, and only when it is not "both", so a
  build repository whose workflow predates the input keeps accepting
  default builds. The JSON API takes macArch with the same choices.
- The workflow side (pullify, patches 0008/0009) builds the Mac matrix
  from mac_arch, and sends each Mac job to the runner label in the
  repository variable RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_X86_64 or _AARCH64, so the
  Mac jobs can run on a self-hosted Mac, where they cost no minutes.
- The cost note next to the platform follows the choice.
- SETUP-PULL.md: costs per platform, a budget, and how to set up a Mac
  of your own as the runner.

The GitHub API stub accepts the macOS workflow's optional input and
still rejects anything undeclared, as GitHub does.

